Perhaps what you need to look at, is how to Convert a
SpatialGridDataFrame to a matrix (or to an array if there are more than
one bands). It seems that biOps uses simple matrices/arrays for its
image objects. if you google it you should find some   responses to
earlier requests send to R-SIG-geo.
 
alternatively, you could import directly to biOps your image as tiff
from your system's disk space.
hth,
